IMPORT `cb1-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part VI, sections 46 and 47: the sale of
-- constrained shares by the corporation and the trust fund that holds the proceeds. Layer 1: the law,
-- objectively.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Each rule is named `<what it decides> within s <section>`. The conditions, the notice and
-- the manner of investing that the Act leaves to the regulations ("that may be prescribed") are plain inputs.

§ `Part VI -- Sale of constrained shares (s 46 and s 47)`

§§ `s 46 sale of constrained shares`

-- s 46(1): a corporation that has constraints on the issue, transfer or ownership of its shares may, for one of
-- three purposes, sell as if it were the owner any of those constrained shares "that are owned, or that the
-- directors determine in the manner that may be prescribed may be owned, contrary to the constraints",
-- "under the conditions and after giving the notice that may be prescribed". The directors' choice to sell is
-- theirs; the rule says whether the corporation may.
-- src:671 | 46 (1) A corporation that has constraints on the issue, transfer or ownership of its shares of any class or series may, for any of the purposes referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c), sell, under the conditions and after giving the notice that may be prescribed, as if it were the owner of the shares, any of those constrained shares that are owned, or that the directors determine in the manner that may be prescribed may be owned, contrary to the constraints in order to
-- src:672 | (a) assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under any prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control;
-- src:673 | (b) assist the corporation to comply with any prescribed law; or
-- src:674 | (c) attain or maintain a level of Canadian ownership specified in its articles.
@ref CBCA s 46(1) sale of constrained shares by corporation (src:671-674)
DECLARE `Purpose of a sale of constrained shares (s 46(1))` IS ONE OF
    `to assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under a prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control`
    `to assist the corporation to comply with a prescribed law`
    `to attain or maintain a level of Canadian ownership specified in its articles`
    `any other purpose`

-- src:671 | 46 (1) A corporation that has constraints on the issue, transfer or ownership of its shares of any class or series may, for any of the purposes referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c), sell, under the conditions and after giving the notice that may be prescribed, as if it were the owner of the shares, any of those constrained shares that are owned, or that the directors determine in the manner that may be prescribed may be owned, contrary to the constraints in order to
-- src:672 | (a) assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under any prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control;
-- src:673 | (b) assist the corporation to comply with any prescribed law; or
-- src:674 | (c) attain or maintain a level of Canadian ownership specified in its articles.
@ref CBCA s 46(1) sale of constrained shares by corporation (src:671-674)
GIVEN purpose IS A `Purpose of a sale of constrained shares (s 46(1))`
      `the corporation has constraints on the issue, transfer or ownership of its shares of the class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are owned, or the directors have determined in the prescribed manner that they may be owned, contrary to the constraints` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the prescribed conditions are met and the prescribed notice has been given` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may sell the constrained shares as if it were their owner within s 46(1)` MEANS
        `the corporation has constraints on the issue, transfer or ownership of its shares of the class or series`
    AND `the shares are owned, or the directors have determined in the prescribed manner that they may be owned, contrary to the constraints`
    AND `the prescribed conditions are met and the prescribed notice has been given`
    AND CONSIDER purpose
        WHEN `to assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under a prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `to assist the corporation to comply with a prescribed law` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `to attain or maintain a level of Canadian ownership specified in its articles` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `any other purpose` THEN FALSE

-- s 46(2): the directors "shall select the shares for sale in good faith and in a manner that is not unfairly
-- prejudicial to, and does not unfairly disregard the interests of, the holders of the shares in the
-- constrained class or series taken as a whole."
-- src:676 | (2) Where shares are to be sold by a corporation under subsection (1), the directors of the corporation shall select the shares for sale in good faith and in a manner that is not unfairly prejudicial to, and does not unfairly disregard the interests of, the holders of the shares in the constrained class or series taken as a whole.
@ref CBCA s 46(2) obligations of directors in sale (src:676)
GIVEN `the directors selected the shares for sale in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the selection is unfairly prejudicial to the holders of the shares in the constrained class or series taken as a whole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the selection unfairly disregards the interests of those holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors have complied with the duty in selecting the shares for sale within s 46(2)` MEANS
        `the directors selected the shares for sale in good faith`
    AND (NOT `the selection is unfairly prejudicial to the holders of the shares in the constrained class or series taken as a whole`)
    AND (NOT `the selection unfairly disregards the interests of those holders`)

-- s 46(3): the owner immediately before the sale "shall by that sale be divested of their interest or right in
-- the shares"; the person who would otherwise be the registered owner, or who satisfies the corporation that
-- they could properly be treated as the registered owner or holder under section 51, "shall, from the time of
-- the sale, be entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale, together with any income earned on the
-- proceeds from the beginning of the month next following the date of the receipt by the corporation of the
-- proceeds of the sale, less any taxes on the proceeds and any costs of administration of a trust fund
-- constituted under subsection 47(1)".
-- src:678 | (3) If shares are sold by a corporation under subsection (1), the owner of the shares immediately before the sale shall by that sale be divested of their interest or right in the shares, and the person who, but for the sale, would be the registered owner of the shares or a person who satisfies the corporation that, but for the sale, they could properly be treated as the registered owner or registered holder of the shares under section 51 shall, from the time of the sale, be entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale, together with any income earned on the proceeds from the beginning of the month next following the date of the receipt by the corporation of the proceeds of the sale, less any taxes on the proceeds and any costs of administration of a trust fund constituted under subsection 47(1) in relation to the constitution of the fund.
@ref CBCA s 46(3) effect of sale (src:678)
GIVEN `the shares were sold under subsection 46(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the owner immediately before the sale is divested of their interest or right in the shares within s 46(3)` MEANS
    `the shares were sold under subsection 46(1)`

-- src:678 | (3) If shares are sold by a corporation under subsection (1), the owner of the shares immediately before the sale shall by that sale be divested of their interest or right in the shares, and the person who, but for the sale, would be the registered owner of the shares or a person who satisfies the corporation that, but for the sale, they could properly be treated as the registered owner or registered holder of the shares under section 51 shall, from the time of the sale, be entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale, together with any income earned on the proceeds from the beginning of the month next following the date of the receipt by the corporation of the proceeds of the sale, less any taxes on the proceeds and any costs of administration of a trust fund constituted under subsection 47(1) in relation to the constitution of the fund.
@ref CBCA s 46(3) effect of sale (src:678)
GIVEN `the net proceeds of the sale, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the income earned on the proceeds from the beginning of the month next following the date of the receipt by the corporation of the proceeds, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the taxes on the proceeds, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs of administration of a trust fund constituted under subsection 47(1) in relation to the constitution of the fund, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the person who would otherwise be the registered owner receives within s 46(3)` MEANS
    (`the net proceeds of the sale, in dollars` PLUS `the income earned on the proceeds from the beginning of the month next following the date of the receipt by the corporation of the proceeds, in dollars`) MINUS `the taxes on the proceeds, in dollars` MINUS `the costs of administration of a trust fund constituted under subsection 47(1) in relation to the constitution of the fund, in dollars`

-- src:678 | (3) If shares are sold by a corporation under subsection (1), the owner of the shares immediately before the sale shall by that sale be divested of their interest or right in the shares, and the person who, but for the sale, would be the registered owner of the shares or a person who satisfies the corporation that, but for the sale, they could properly be treated as the registered owner or registered holder of the shares under section 51 shall, from the time of the sale, be entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale, together with any income earned on the proceeds from the beginning of the month next following the date of the receipt by the corporation of the proceeds of the sale, less any taxes on the proceeds and any costs of administration of a trust fund constituted under subsection 47(1) in relation to the constitution of the fund.
@ref CBCA s 46(3) effect of sale (src:678)
GIVEN `the shares were sold under subsection 46(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would, but for the sale, be the registered owner of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person satisfies the corporation that, but for the sale, they could properly be treated as the registered owner or registered holder of the shares under section 51` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 51 (piece cb2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale within s 46(3)` MEANS
        `the shares were sold under subsection 46(1)`
    AND (    `the person would, but for the sale, be the registered owner of the shares`
          OR `the person satisfies the corporation that, but for the sale, they could properly be treated as the registered owner or registered holder of the shares under section 51`)

-- src:680 | (4) Subsections 51(4) to (6) apply in respect of the person who is entitled under subsection (3) to receive the proceeds of a sale of shares under subsection (1) as if the proceeds were a security and the person were a registered holder or owner of the security.
@ref CBCA s 46(4) subsections 51(4) to (6) apply (src:680)
GIVEN `the person is entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of a sale of shares under subsection 46(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsections 51(4) to (6) apply to the person as if the proceeds were a security and the person were a registered holder or owner within s 46(4)` MEANS
    `the person is entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of a sale of shares under subsection 46(1)`

§§ `s 47 proceeds of sale; trust fund`

-- src:682 | 47 (1) The proceeds of a sale by a corporation under subsection 46(1) constitute a trust fund in the hands of the corporation for the benefit of the person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of the sale, and any such trust fund may be commingled by the corporation with other such trust funds and shall be invested in such manner as may be prescribed.
@ref CBCA s 47(1) proceeds of sale to be trust fund (src:682)
GIVEN `the proceeds are the proceeds of a sale by the corporation under subsection 46(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proceeds constitute a trust fund in the hands of the corporation within s 47(1)` MEANS
    `the proceeds are the proceeds of a sale by the corporation under subsection 46(1)`

-- src:682 | 47 (1) The proceeds of a sale by a corporation under subsection 46(1) constitute a trust fund in the hands of the corporation for the benefit of the person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of the sale, and any such trust fund may be commingled by the corporation with other such trust funds and shall be invested in such manner as may be prescribed.
@ref CBCA s 47(1) proceeds of sale to be trust fund (src:682)
GIVEN `the fund is invested in the manner that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the trust fund has been invested as s 47(1) requires` MEANS
    `the fund is invested in the manner that may be prescribed`

-- src:684 | (2) Reasonable costs of administration of a trust fund referred to in subsection (1) may be deducted from the trust fund and any income earned thereon.
@ref CBCA s 47(2) costs of administration (src:684)
GIVEN `the costs are reasonable costs of administration of a trust fund referred to in subsection 47(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may deduct the costs from the trust fund and any income earned thereon within s 47(2)` MEANS
    `the costs are reasonable costs of administration of a trust fund referred to in subsection 47(1)`

-- src:686 | (3) Subject to this section, a corporation may transfer any trust fund referred to in subsection (1), and the administration thereof, to a trust company in Canada registered as such under the laws of Canada or a province, and the corporation is thereupon discharged of all further liability in respect of the trust fund.
@ref CBCA s 47(3) appointment of trust company (src:686)
GIVEN `the transferee is a trust company in Canada registered as such under the laws of Canada or a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may transfer the trust fund and its administration to the transferee within s 47(3)` MEANS
    `the transferee is a trust company in Canada registered as such under the laws of Canada or a province`

-- src:686 | (3) Subject to this section, a corporation may transfer any trust fund referred to in subsection (1), and the administration thereof, to a trust company in Canada registered as such under the laws of Canada or a province, and the corporation is thereupon discharged of all further liability in respect of the trust fund.
@ref CBCA s 47(3) appointment of trust company (src:686)
GIVEN `the corporation transferred the trust fund, and the administration of it, to a trust company under subsection 47(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is discharged of all further liability in respect of the trust fund within s 47(3)` MEANS
    `the corporation transferred the trust fund, and the administration of it, to a trust company under subsection 47(3)`

-- src:688 | (4) A receipt signed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of a sale that constitute a trust fund under subsection (1) shall be a complete discharge of the corporation and of any trust company to which a trust fund is transferred under subsection (3), in respect of the trust fund and income earned thereon paid to such person.
@ref CBCA s 47(4) discharge of corporation and trust company (src:688)
GIVEN `the receipt is signed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the receipt is a complete discharge of the corporation and of any trust company within s 47(4)` MEANS
    `the receipt is signed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of the sale`

-- s 47(5): a trust fund (with its income, less taxes and costs) "that has not been claimed ... for a period of ten
-- years after the date of the sale vests in Her Majesty in right of Canada". Ten years counted from the date of
-- the sale by the keel's convention (F1): the fund has vested once the last day has passed without a claim.
-- src:690 | (5) A trust fund described in subsection (1), together with any income earned thereon, less any taxes thereon and costs of administration, that has not been claimed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of a sale that constitute the trust fund for a period of ten years after the date of the sale vests in Her Majesty in right of Canada.
@ref CBCA s 47(5) vesting in Crown (src:690)
DECIDE `the ten-year period of s 47(5)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 10
    `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:690 | (5) A trust fund described in subsection (1), together with any income earned thereon, less any taxes thereon and costs of administration, that has not been claimed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of a sale that constitute the trust fund for a period of ten years after the date of the sale vests in Her Majesty in right of Canada.
@ref CBCA s 47(5) vesting in Crown (src:690)
GIVEN `the date of the sale` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the fund can be claimed before it vests in the Crown within s 47(5)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the ten-year period of s 47(5)` `counted from` `the date of the sale`

-- src:690 | (5) A trust fund described in subsection (1), together with any income earned thereon, less any taxes thereon and costs of administration, that has not been claimed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of a sale that constitute the trust fund for a period of ten years after the date of the sale vests in Her Majesty in right of Canada.
@ref CBCA s 47(5) vesting in Crown (src:690)
GIVEN `the date of the sale` IS A DATE
      `the fund has been claimed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the fund has vested in Her Majesty in right of Canada on the day within s 47(5)` MEANS
        (NOT `the fund has been claimed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of the sale`)
    AND (NOT (`done within the time limit` `the ten-year period of s 47(5)` `the date of the sale` day))
    AND day AT LEAST `the date of the sale`

-- src:692 | (6) Sections 3 to 5 of the Escheats Act apply in respect of a trust fund that vests in Her Majesty in right of Canada under subsection (5).
@ref CBCA s 47(6) Escheats Act applies (src:692)
GIVEN `the fund has vested in Her Majesty in right of Canada under subsection 47(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sections 3 to 5 of the Escheats Act apply to the fund within s 47(6)` MEANS
    `the fund has vested in Her Majesty in right of Canada under subsection 47(5)`
